@startuml fig2_algorithm_view
' Diagram 2 of the ISO/IEC 22989 pattern: algorithms, models and parameters.
'
' Conventions: shared/FIGURES.md. Flat boxes, no namespace prefixes, no clause
' numbers, orthogonal edges, nothing explanatory inside the drawing.
'
' What it shows: the second of the three views. The distinction the pattern
' turns on, between a procedure and a model, and between the parameters chosen
' in advance and those a training determines.
'
' The two pairs to read together:
'
'   Model      is what MLModel is a case of, and only the second is learned
'   Parameter  is either chosen before training or determined by it
'
' Left out on purpose:
'  - the system, its tasks and its functions: diagram 1
'  - data and the processes preparing it: diagram 3
'  - the qualities of clause 3.5: diagram 4
'
' Only the machine learning algorithm has an entry in clause 3. The superclass
' and the other two kinds are constructs of this work, which REFERENCE.md
' records apart from the entries.

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 45
skinparam padding 3
skinparam ArrowColor #1A2733
skinparam ArrowFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1A2733
hide empty members
hide circle
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FCEFC7
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontColor #1A2733
  FontSize 14
  BorderThickness 1
}

' ===================================================================
'  The procedures
' ===================================================================

class Algorithm
class ModelAlgorithm
class TrainingAlgorithm
class MLAlgorithm
class EvaluationAlgorithm
class EvaluationMetric

Algorithm <|-- ModelAlgorithm
Algorithm <|-- TrainingAlgorithm
Algorithm <|-- EvaluationAlgorithm
TrainingAlgorithm <|-- MLAlgorithm

EvaluationAlgorithm --> "*" EvaluationMetric : usesMetric

' ===================================================================
'  What kind of learning
' ===================================================================

class LearningType
class SupervisedLearning
class UnsupervisedLearning
class SemiSupervisedLearning
class ReinforcementLearning

LearningType <|-- SupervisedLearning
LearningType <|-- UnsupervisedLearning
LearningType <|-- SemiSupervisedLearning
LearningType <|-- ReinforcementLearning

MLAlgorithm --> "1" LearningType : basedOnLearning

' ===================================================================
'  The models
' ===================================================================

class Model
class MLModel

Model <|-- MLModel

Model --> "*" Algorithm : basedOnAlgorithm

' ===================================================================
'  The two kinds of parameter
' ===================================================================

class Hyperparameter
class ModelParameter
class CharacteristicValue

Algorithm --> "*" Hyperparameter : hasHyperparameter
Model     --> "*" ModelParameter : hasParameter

' The value a hyperparameter was set to. Reached by a relation of its own
' rather than by forCharacteristic, since it is chosen before a training
' whereas a quality of clause 3.5 is established by one. Diagram 4 shows the
' other way into the same class.
Hyperparameter --> "1" CharacteristicValue : hasSetting

' ===================================================================
'  What produces a model, and what a model does
' ===================================================================

class Training
class MachineLearning
class Retraining
class Inference
class Prediction
class Validation
class Evaluation

Training <|-- MachineLearning
Training <|-- Retraining

Training  --> "*" ModelParameter : determines
MLModel   --> "*" Training       : isCreatedBy
Model     --> "*" Validation     : isValidatedBy
Model     --> "*" Evaluation     : isEvaluatedBy
Inference --> "*" Model          : isExecutedBy
Inference --> "*" Prediction     : creates

' Layout only: keep each fan of siblings on one row.
ModelAlgorithm -[hidden]right- TrainingAlgorithm
TrainingAlgorithm -[hidden]right- EvaluationAlgorithm

SupervisedLearning -[hidden]right- UnsupervisedLearning
UnsupervisedLearning -[hidden]right- SemiSupervisedLearning
SemiSupervisedLearning -[hidden]right- ReinforcementLearning

MachineLearning -[hidden]right- Retraining

@enduml
